# Analysis of the professor's dashboard (FINA 405 — `Project_CP1.html`)
Saved copy: `01_Brief/professor_dashboard/` (HTML files from his public repo https://luisceballos.github.io/FINA405-Dashboard/ ; HAL object extracted to `01_Brief/professor_dashboard/HAL/`; HAL/Kuwait series exported to `08_Assets/data/prof_dashboard_*.csv`). Reviewed live in the browser (1440×900) and from source. Instructor-mode (password + Firestore) was **not** touched.
Context from Canvas mail (Prof. Ceballos, 18–27 Sep 2026): the dashboard is the instructor's *"Dashboard actualizado — Empresa asignada"* for Project Check-in 1 (Sections 1 & 2); CP1 deck was due 30-Sep (format free; 4 random teams present 10 min each); **the 21-Oct video is judged by an external jury on content *and* presentation quality**; "think visually"; the last slide must answer *how the country's macro environment affects the firm's financing strategy*; the project note says **teams will demonstrate a live scenario in the final presentation**.

## 1. What it is
Single-file HTML app (≈ 2.4 MB, all data embedded in a JS object `ALL_DATA`), **22 firms** (11 assigned groups G1–G11 + 11 "SAMPLE" firms), one scrolling page per firm, switcher buttons (`switchFirm('HAL')`). Libraries: Plotly 2.27.1 (charts), Firebase 9.23 Firestore (instructor notes, document `fina405_dashboard/instructor`), Google Fonts (Libre Baskerville for headings, DM Sans for body). Light/dark via `prefers-color-scheme`, breakpoints 600/760/900/960 px. Data sources shown in footnotes: Yahoo Finance, World Bank, FRED, SEC EDGAR 10-K text (risk excerpts).

## 2. Page anatomy (HAL view)
1. **Hero band (navy #1A3A6B, gold rule #C4901A):** ticker + name (serif), sector/industry/exchange/country, instructor tag, timestamp. Two KPI rows — *Company:* last price, YTD, market cap, P/E, beta, revenue (LTM), net margin, D/E; *Country:* GDP growth, CPI, local-ccy/USD, FX change (2y), sovereign rating, FX regime.
2. **Three risk cards:** FX risk of issuing in the country (LOW–MEDIUM…), interest-rate/sovereign risk, hedging instruments (FX forwards per coupon, CCS if tenor > 2y, IRS+FRA).
3. **Risk Analysis Assessment box:** verbatim 10-K excerpts on FX (for HAL: *"10-K data not available. Run the script with --tickers HAL to fetch it."* → empty).
4. **Business overview + debt structure:** description, total assets/equity/D/E/interest coverage/current ratio/net debt-EBITDA, debt tiles (total, LT, ST, LT %, debt/assets) + generated paragraph on currency/maturity/serviceability.
5. **Charts:** balance-sheet evolution (bars + total debt line), leverage & liquidity (D/E, current ratio), geographic revenue mix (pie).
6. **Company analysis:** 3-yr stock price with MA50/MA200, annual financials (revenue/EBITDA/net income), return & margin trends, KPI tiles (EBIT/net margin, ROE, ROA), **peer table** (HAL vs SLB, BKR, NOV: market cap, P/E, P/B, beta, div yield).
7. **Country overview:** narrative paragraph, KPI tiles (GDP, CPI, current account, unemployment, FX, policy rate, 10y yield, term spread, CDS range, stance badge), charts: GDP growth, CPI, FX 2y, local-gov spread vs UST, policy vs 10y, current account.
8. **Instructor mode (🔐):** SHA-256 password gate, per-firm comment/rating fields saved to Firestore.

## 3. Strengths worth copying
* Strict, repeatable structure per firm (same KPIs, same chart set) → easy to compare and grade.
* Hero KPI band + three risk cards: instantly answers "how big is the exposure and what instrument fits".
* Each chart has a source footnote; data tied to primary sources (10-K, WB, FRED, Yahoo).
* Responsive and dark-mode aware; plain HTML = trivially hostable.

